> show 1 + 2i + 3j + 4k
  note: i, j, k are the quaternion units: i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1, ij = k = -ji (say k: real for a variable k)
_() = 2i + 1 + 3j + 4k
  -> quaternion
> show re(1 + 2i + 3j + 4k)
  note: i, j, k are the quaternion units: i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1, ij = k = -ji (say k: real for a variable k)
_() = re(2i + 1 + 3j + 4k)
  -> quaternion
> show q: quat
_(q: quaternion) = q
  -> quaternion
> show i
_() = i
  -> complex
> show j
  note: j is read as the imaginary unit (j^2 = -1)
_() = i
  -> complex
> show cd(1)
  note: 'cd' read as c*d (single-letter variables)
_(c: real, d: real) = c*d
  -> real
> show cd(2)
  note: 'cd' read as c*d (single-letter variables)
_(c: real, d: real) = 2(c*d)
  -> real
> show cd(16)
  note: 'cd' read as c*d (single-letter variables)
_(c: real, d: real) = 16(c*d)
  -> real
> show table cd(8)
  note: 'cd' read as c*d (single-letter variables)
_(table: real, c: real, d: real) = 8(table*(c*d))
  -> real
